// Cedar schema of the second official sample (team-docs).
//
// Several users belong to an org (workspace) as owner / editor / viewer; documents are shared within the org and can
// also be shared with individual users. Documents have creation and update times, which are recorded only if they are
// the current time nyxis determines per request (`context.now`) (policies.cedar).
//
// In nyxis this document doubles as the table definition: - entity type = table, attribute = column, entity ID =
// primary key (there is no mapping code). - Each action carries one effect with `@effect("…")` (the operation that
// happens in the DB when permitted).
// - Membership is represented by rows of a separate table (membership rows): a `Membership` row states that "user user
// belongs to team team of org org", and `entity User in [Team, Org]` with
// `@memberships("Membership: user -> team, org")` declares that a user entity has the team and org values of its own
// membership rows as parents (Cedar ancestors). Policies can write `principal in resource.org` (if the principal is a
// member of the resource's org) and `principal in resource.org.editors` (if the principal belongs to the editor team of
// the resource's org). Many-to-many membership (one person in several orgs, one org with several people) is expressed
// by as many membership rows as needed.
// - A team (`Team`) is a per-org role team; an org references exactly one editor team and one viewer team. owner is
// held as the org row's set of users (`owners`) (a few administrators who can change memberships and delete the org).
// - `entity Doc in [Org]` with `@parents("org")` declares that a document entity has the value of column `org` (the
// org) as parent. - A `Set<User>` column is a set of entities (the set of owners, the individual share targets).
// - The `context` of insert and update actions contains the proposed values `values`, and for actions that declare
// `now`, `context.now` contains the current time nyxis determined (the handler cannot forge it).
// - `@unique("column, …")` is uniqueness of a tuple of columns (org names are unique, document titles are unique within
// an org, team roles are unique within an org, one membership row per (user, team) pair). A violation is 409.
// - `@references("column restrict, column cascade action")` is referential integrity of entity reference columns: an
// insert or update whose referenced row is missing is 409. Deleting a referenced row is 409 under `restrict` if
// referencing rows exist (a user who created documents cannot be deleted); under `cascade` the referencing rows are
// deleted too (deleting an org also deletes its teams, membership rows and documents; deleting a user deletes its
// membership rows). Each deleted row is judged by that action (`deleteTeam` / `removeMember` / `deleteDoc`), and if
// even one row is not permitted the whole request becomes 403 and nothing is deleted. nyxis also sets the same
// constraints in the DB.
// - Attachments: a document can have one attachment file in Supabase Storage. `@attachment("attachment")` names the
// String column that stores the attachment object's name (a unique ID issued by nyxis) (the empty string means no
// attachment). `@effect("upload Doc")` / `@effect("download Doc")` are declared external effects: only when permitted
// does nyxis request issuance of a signed URL for the Storage object `Doc/<document primary key>/<name>` (`context.id`
// for uploads, the value of column `attachment` for downloads). The handler can name neither the path nor the bucket,
// and file contents do not pass through nyxis.
// - Notifications: a user can subscribe to a document (`Subscription`; the recipient mail address is the column `email`
// the user writes when subscribing; it is not read from Auth), and when the document is shared, a notification row
// (`Notification`: recipient, subject, body, whether sent) is created per subscriber and mail is sent.
// `@effect("mail Notification(email; subject, body)")` is a declared external effect: only when permitted does nyxis
// send to the SMTP relay of the core settings, with the row's column `email` as recipient, `subject` as subject and
// `body` as body. The handler can name neither the recipient nor the content. Sending does not change the DB (the sent
// record is a separate action `markNotificationSent`).
// - `Service` is the service principal type reserved by nyxis (not a table). It is the principal of the periodic job
// (`TeamDocs.Jobs.notifyPending`: sends, among the unsent notifications, only those whose recipient user can read the
// document now), and its ID is determined by the core setting `NYXIS_SERVICE_PRINCIPAL`. It never becomes the principal
// of an HTTP request (the principal of a JWT is always a `User`).
// - `Anonymous` is the principal type reserved by nyxis, the principal of requests without a JWT or whose verification
// failed. Not a table.
// - External API calls: `Summarizer` / `Audit`, annotated with `@external("base: …; auth: …")`, are named destinations
// (a kind reserved by nyxis: not tables, with no attributes or parents, and not allowed in `appliesTo`). The base URL
// and authentication scheme are written here; the keys are the core settings `NYXIS_EXT_SUMMARIZER` / `NYXIS_EXT_AUDIT`
// (environment variables; the approved source has only their names). `@effect("call …")` is a declared external effect:
// only when permitted does nyxis send the URL and body it determined from the approved declaration and the target row's
// columns alone (the handler can build neither the URL, the headers nor the body). `sync` (`summarizeDoc`) decodes the
// response into the type declared in the approved source and passes it to the handler as a value; the handler writes it
// to the DB through a separate action (`recordSummary`) — that write passes the ordinary decision. `async`
// (`announceDocUpdate`) has no response; it is written to nyxis's reserved table `_nyxis_outbox` in the same
// transaction, and nyxis's internal loop sends it after COMMIT. Both destinations of this sample are a local mock API
// (started by `scripts/check-team-docs.py` at https://localhost:18118), not production URLs.
//
// Developers read and approve this document and policies.cedar.

// A user. The Supabase Auth user ID becomes the entity ID (primary key). Has the team and org of its membership rows
// (Membership) as parents.
@memberships("Membership: user -> team, org")
entity User in [Team, Org] = {
  "name": String
};

// An org. owner is held as a set of users (who can change memberships and delete the org); editor and viewer are each
// held as one team (Team) (team membership is Membership rows). Org names are unique.
@unique("name")
entity Org = {
  "name": String,
  "owners": Set<User>,
  "editors": Team,
  "viewers": Team
};

// A role team of an org. The role is unique within the org (one editor team and one viewer team per org). Deleting the
// org deletes its teams.
@unique("org, role")
@references("org cascade deleteTeam")
entity Team = {
  "org": Org,
  "role": String
};

// Membership row: user user belongs to team team of org org. One row per (user, team) pair. If the user, team or org is
// deleted, the membership row is deleted (each row judged by removeMember).
@unique("user, team")
@references("user cascade removeMember, team cascade removeMember, org cascade removeMember")
entity Membership = {
  "user": User,
  "team": Team,
  "org": Org
};

// A document. Has an org as parent and can have individual share targets (shared). Titles are unique within an org.
// Deleting the org deletes the documents (each judged by deleteDoc), and a user who created documents cannot be
// deleted. The attachment name is column attachment (the empty string means no attachment). summary is the value
// recorded by recordSummary from the response of the external summarizer API (Summarizer) (the empty string means no
// summary).
@parents("org")
@unique("org, title")
@references("org cascade deleteDoc, createdBy restrict")
@attachment("attachment")
entity Doc in [Org] = {
  "org": Org,
  "title": String,
  "body": String,
  "shared": Set<User>,
  "createdBy": User,
  "createdAt": datetime,
  "updatedAt": datetime,
  "attachment": String,
  "summary": String
};

// Subscription: user user receives notifications of sharing of document doc. The recipient mail address is written when
// subscribing. One row per (user, document) pair. Deleting the document or user deletes the subscription (each row
// judged by deleteSubscription).
@unique("doc, user")
@references("doc cascade deleteSubscription, user cascade deleteSubscription")
entity Subscription = {
  "doc": Doc,
  "user": User,
  "email": String
};

// Notification: a sending record created per subscriber when a document is shared. It points at the original
// subscription (subscription), and the policy requires that the recipient (email) and recipient user (recipient) match
// that subscription's columns and that the subject (subject) and body (body) match the document's title and body (at
// creation and at sending). The mail-sending effect uses this row's column values as they are. sent is whether it was
// sent. Deleting the document, the recipient user or the subscription deletes the notification.
@references("doc cascade deleteNotification, recipient cascade deleteNotification, subscription cascade deleteNotification")
entity Notification = {
  "doc": Doc,
  "recipient": User,
  "subscription": Subscription,
  "email": String,
  "subject": String,
  "body": String,
  "sent": Bool
};

// The anonymous principal (reserved by nyxis; not a table).
entity Anonymous;

// The service principal (reserved by nyxis; not a table). The principal of periodic jobs; never the principal of an
// HTTP request.
entity Service;

// External API destinations (a kind reserved by nyxis; not tables). The document summarizer API (sync) and the document
// update audit log API (async). Both are a local mock API (started by the integration test). The keys are the
// environment variables NYXIS_EXT_SUMMARIZER / NYXIS_EXT_AUDIT.
@external("base: https://localhost:18118/summarizer; auth: bearer NYXIS_EXT_SUMMARIZER")
entity Summarizer;

@external("base: https://localhost:18118/audit; auth: bearer NYXIS_EXT_AUDIT")
entity Audit;

// Registers a user (creates one's own User row).
@effect("insert User")
action "registerUser" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [User],
  context: { "values": { "name": String } }
};

// Reads a user. The user themselves only.
@effect("read User")
action "readUser" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [User]
};

// Deletes a user (one's own User row). Membership rows are deleted by cascade. A user who created documents cannot be
// deleted, by referential integrity (restrict) (409).
@effect("delete User")
action "deleteUser" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [User]
};

// Creates an org. The creator becomes its only owner, and the editor and viewer teams point at teams that do not exist
// yet (created next by createTeam).
@effect("insert Org")
action "createOrg" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Org],
  context: { "values": { "name": String, "owners": Set<User>, "editors": Team, "viewers": Team } }
};

// Reads an org. Only owners and users who belong to one of its teams.
@effect("read Org")
action "readOrg" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Org]
};

// Lists the orgs one belongs to.
@effect("list Org")
action "listOrgs" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Org]
};

// Deletes an org. Owners only. Teams, membership rows and documents are deleted by cascade, each document judged by
// deleteDoc (cannot delete if someone else's documents remain).
@effect("delete Org")
action "deleteOrg" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Org]
};

// Changes the org's set of owners. Owners only. An owner cannot remove themselves.
@effect("update Org(owners)")
action "setOwners" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Org],
  context: { "values": { "owners"?: Set<User> } }
};

// Creates a role team of an org. Owners of the org only. Limited to the team the org references as the team of that
// role.
@effect("insert Team")
action "createTeam" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Team],
  context: { "values": { "org": Org, "role": String } }
};

// Deletes a team (the cascade of an org deletion judges each team with this). Owners of the org only.
@effect("delete Team")
action "deleteTeam" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Team]
};

// Adds a user to a team of an org (creates a membership row). Owners of the org only. The team must be a team of that
// org.
@effect("insert Membership")
action "addMember" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Membership],
  context: { "values": { "user": User, "team": Team, "org": Org } }
};

// Lists the org's membership rows. Only owners and users who belong to one of its teams.
@effect("list Membership")
action "listMembers" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Membership]
};

// Deletes a membership row (the cascades of org, team and user deletions also judge each membership row with this). The
// member themselves or an owner of the org.
@effect("delete Membership")
action "removeMember" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Membership]
};

// Creates a document. Only owners of the org and users in the editor team. Creation and update times are nyxis's
// current time (context.now). No attachment and no summary.
@effect("insert Doc")
action "createDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: {
    "values": {
      "org": Org, "title": String, "body": String, "shared": Set<User>,
      "createdBy": User, "createdAt": datetime, "updatedAt": datetime, "attachment": String, "summary": String
    },
    "now": datetime
  }
};

// Reads a document. Owners of the org, users who belong to a team of the org, individually shared users.
@effect("read Doc")
action "readDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Lists documents. Applies the same condition as readDoc to each row.
@effect("list Doc")
action "listDocs" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Edits a document's title and body. The update time must be nyxis's current time.
@effect("update Doc(title, body, updatedAt)")
action "editDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: {
    "values": { "title"?: String, "body"?: String, "updatedAt"?: datetime },
    "now": datetime
  }
};

// Asks the external summarizer API for a document summary (an external effect; sync). Only owners of the org and users
// in the editor team. When permitted, nyxis sends the document's title and body to Summarizer's POST
// /v1/summaries/<document primary key>, decodes the response into { summary: String } and passes it to the handler
// (5-second deadline). The response is not written to the DB; the handler records it separately through recordSummary,
// which passes its own decision.
@effect("call Summarizer POST /v1/summaries/{key} Doc(title, body) sync 5s -> { summary: String }")
action "summarizeDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Records a summary (the only path for writing an external API response value). Only owners of the org and users in the
// editor team. An empty summary cannot be recorded.
@effect("update Doc(summary)")
action "recordSummary" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: { "values": { "summary"?: String } }
};

// Announces a document update to the audit log API (an external effect; async). Only owners of the org and users in the
// editor team. When permitted, nyxis writes the document's title and update time for Audit's POST /v1/docs/<document
// primary key>/updated to the outbox in the request's own transaction, and the internal loop sends it after COMMIT
// (there is no response).
@effect("call Audit POST /v1/docs/{key}/updated Doc(title, updatedAt) async")
action "announceDocUpdate" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Shares a document with individual users (replaces the set of share targets). Only owners of the org and users in the
// editor team.
@effect("update Doc(shared)")
action "shareDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: { "values": { "shared"?: Set<User> } }
};

// Deletes a document. Its creator only (while they remain an owner of the org or in the editor team). The cascade of an
// org deletion also judges each document with this.
@effect("delete Doc")
action "deleteDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Records the attachment name (just before issuing the upload URL, writes the unique ID issued by nyxis to column
// attachment). Only owners of the org and users in the editor team. The name that can be recorded is limited to this
// request's unique ID (context.id).
@effect("update Doc(attachment)")
action "attachDoc" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: { "values": { "attachment"?: String }, "id": String }
};

// Issues a signed upload URL for the attachment (an external effect). Only owners of the org and users in the editor
// team, and only when the attachment name recorded in the document is this request's unique ID (the issuance target is
// Doc/<document>/<context.id>).
@effect("upload Doc")
action "uploadAttachment" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc],
  context: { "id": String }
};

// Issues a signed download URL for the attachment (an external effect). Users who can read the document (owners of the
// org, users who belong to a team of the org, individually shared users). The issuance target is Doc/<document>/<value
// of column attachment>.
@effect("download Doc")
action "downloadAttachment" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Doc]
};

// Subscribes to a document (creates one's own subscription row). Only users who can read the document. The recipient
// mail address is given in the body.
@effect("insert Subscription")
action "subscribe" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Subscription],
  context: { "values": { "doc": Doc, "user": User, "email": String } }
};

// Lists a document's subscriptions. One's own subscriptions, and owners of the document's org and users in its editor
// team (to collect recipients when sharing).
@effect("list Subscription")
action "listSubscriptions" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Subscription]
};

// Unsubscribes. The subscriber, the document's creator, or an owner of the document's org (the cascades of document and
// user deletions also judge each row with this).
@effect("delete Subscription")
action "deleteSubscription" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Subscription]
};

// Creates a notification row (per subscriber when a document is shared). Only owners of the document's org and users in
// its editor team. The recipient and recipient user are the referenced subscription's columns, the subject and body are
// the document's title and body, and the row is not yet sent (policy).
@effect("insert Notification")
action "createNotification" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Notification],
  context: { "values": { "doc": Doc, "recipient": User, "subscription": Subscription, "email": String, "subject": String, "body": String, "sent": Bool } }
};

// Sends notification mail (an external effect). The recipient is column email, the subject column subject, the body
// column body. Owners of the document's org and users in its editor team, or the service principal (periodic job). Only
// when not yet sent, the recipient and recipient user match the referenced subscription's columns, and the recipient
// user can read the document now.
@effect("mail Notification(email; subject, body)")
action "sendNotification" appliesTo {
  principal: [User, Service],
  resource: [Notification]
};

// Marks a notification as sent. Owners of the document's org and users in its editor team, or the service principal.
@effect("update Notification(sent)")
action "markNotificationSent" appliesTo {
  principal: [User, Service],
  resource: [Notification],
  context: { "values": { "sent"?: Bool } }
};

// Lists notifications. The service principal (the periodic job collects unsent notifications), and owners of the
// document's org and users in its editor team.
@effect("list Notification")
action "listNotifications" appliesTo {
  principal: [User, Service],
  resource: [Notification]
};

// Deletes a notification (the cascades of document and user deletions judge each row with this). Its recipient, the
// document's creator, or an owner of the document's org.
@effect("delete Notification")
action "deleteNotification" appliesTo {
  principal: [User],
  resource: [Notification]
};
